 "pg.2af9344935": "<b>Vortex phase mask.</b> A transparent mask whose phase winds around its centre (e^(2iθ), charge {n0}) moves an on-axis star's light outside the re-imaged pupil: for an ideal charge-{n1} vortex on a clear circular aperture the field there is exactly zero inside the pupil and ({n2}/ρ)² outside it [calc], so a stop just inside the pupil removes the star. Phase masks are the family that works closest to the star (Mawet et al. {n3}); real vortices leave residuals from wavefront errors and the star's finite size.",
