 "pg.8361fd20c7": "Stylised plate of Lyot&#x27;s coronagraph, in order: parallel starlight enters an objective lens and is focused onto a small opaque occulting disc, which blocks the star&#x27;s image; a field lens re-images the telescope&#x27;s pupil, where the light the disc diffracted lands on the pupil&#x27;s rim; a slightly smaller Lyot stop removes that rim; a camera lens forms the final image, in which a faint companion&#x27;s light, which missed the disc, survives. Insets show the star&#x27;s image with the disc, the pupil with its bright rim inside the stop, and the final image with the companion.",
