 "pg.ed3310fdca": "Four scenes. Transit timing: two planets near a {n0} period ratio tug each other, so the inner planet&#x27;s transits arrive early and late and an O−C diagram builds up. Secondary eclipse: the planet slips behind its star half an orbit after transit, a much smaller dip, drawn ten times deeper. Phase curve: a tidally locked planet shows more of its hot day side towards occultation, with its peak shifted by winds. Rossiter–McLaughlin: the planet covers the approaching and then the receding half of the rotating star, so the star&#x27;s measured velocity swings during transit.",
